# JURNL creative grammar

Source of truth: `shared/studioos-visual-authority/projects/jurnl/bespoke-composition-grammar.ts`
Manifest: `JURNL/MANIFEST/JURNL_CREATIVE_GRAMMAR.json`

Every future JURNL authority — ENTRY, SETUP, TODAY, ACTIVITY, MONEY, INCOME, UPCOMING, PLAN, SAFE TO SPEND, PURCHASES, TRIPS, CREDIT, PAYDOWN, GOALS, AHEAD, RECORDS — is composed at five levels:

1. Composition
2. Environment
3. Artifact
4. Material relationship
5. Graphic expression

A page fails when the direction shows up only as props, paper texture, foliage, or a decorative fragment. A centered paper card on a Mediterranean background is a fail. One stationery object on a generic desk or wall is a fail. Mediterranean rooms, olive, busts, and torn edges are ingredients, not the design system.

The only mark is `public/site00/projects/jurnl/brand/jurnl-logo-official.png`. Do not invent a wordmark, a monogram, a vertical stack, or a substitute botanical. Reserve its region. Do not bake a substitute into the plate.

Every family needs its own room and more than one spatial station. Rotate the camera across the parents. Every parent needs a contrast anchor. A blurred page must still be distinguishable. With the UI copy removed, the frame must still be a JURNL campaign image.

The grammar is shared. The family artifact language is not. Do not make MONEY, CREDIT, PLAN, SETUP, or RECORDS look like ENTRY.

Page authority comes first. The plate keeps the set and removes live UI. Descendants of ENTRY 08–14 stay blocked until the founder approves those parents.
